                <pb facs="0688" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/4459: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-15T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 15,
                                1923—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 15—2:17
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>403. Following from American consul general at Canton: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 14, 2 p.m. …</p>
                        <p>At meeting last evening consular body decided to transmit diplomatic
                            body’s reply to Sun Government today. See senior consul’s telegram of
                            December 13th through the American naval attaché.<anchor n="85"
                                xml:id="d427-f1"/> Consular body also decided to address informal
                            communication to commander in chief Chinese forces warning him that if
                            Sun attempted to seize customs, powers would place marine guards in
                            customshouse without contemplating any infringement Chinese sovereignty,
                            powers being actuated by the utmost friendliness.</p>
                        <p>Plan outlined my telegram of December 10, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="84"
                                xml:id="d427-f2"/> adopted by the consular body. Naval commanders
                            now working out details.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
